"notes": "Governmental funds are modified cash basis (basis=cash); business-type activities are accrual, so proprietary cash-flow block left null (GAAP only). beginning_cash/ending_cash are the governmental funds total fund balances from the revenues/expenditures statement p5 (1,174,478 and 1,519,921); balance sheet p4 shows cash 1,508,069 + county treasurer cash 14,850 = 1,522,919 less payroll withholding liability 2,998. Governmental receipts/disbursements/transfers from the Total Governmental Funds column p5 (transfers net 11,327: Street +21,303; General -3,350 and Debt Service -6,626 out). Business-type lines from p7 Total column; no printed total receipts/expenses, so computed (operating + nonoperating); business-type net position roll-forward: 1,459,584 + 590,864 - 404,894 - 11,327 = 1,634,227. Nonoperating loan forgiveness, interest expense and loan fees are treated as disbursements. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (governmental modified cash plus business-type accrual). General Fund detail uses the combining statement of departments (p14-15, more detailed) by department; the General Fund budget schedule p10 is not recorded to avoid double counting (p10 shows Administrative 267,412, Fire 39,985, Village lights 14,828, environment 206,534; budget Original and Final 534,000 total). Street, Debt Service and Sales Tax detail from budget schedules p11-13. Salaries and benefits combined line mapped to salaries and wages. Read pages 1-15 of 15."
